<!-- Named by port, not by display id, so it applies to both emerald panels.

     This is the stock map from the HyperOS 3 product/etc/displayconfig/display_id_4627039422300187648.xml
     plus the block that lets the framework enter high brightness mode (port of the crDroid line's
     device-tree change `5b19d7e`, verified on C1.8 19.11 with a flashlight: hbmMode=sunlight, backlight
     written above 2047 up to 4095). The map was taken from the OS3.0.307.0 product file; the same
     points (2 / 500 / 1000 nits, minimumLux 6001) were recorded from the stock product file in the
     305 era too, and the vendor part of both stocks is byte-identical, so our 305 base gets the same
     behaviour.

     Scale: the stock lights HAL takes a 12-bit backlight level, our LightsService sends 1..4095
     (frameworks/base, "Send a 12-bit backlight level" - since 2.23 the full panel DBV scale, before
     it was 1..2047), and that level is the panel's DBV, linear with nits: stock minimum DBV 8 is the
     2 nits point, PanelMaxDbv 2047 (end of the factory range, AAL logs "phy:2047/4095" at the slider
     maximum) is 500 nits, and the HBM half of the range ends at DBV 4095 = 1000 nits. Brightness
     values are absolute on that same scale, which is why the settings minimum 1/254 = level 17 sits
     just above MiBrightness MinDBV=16 and the default 0.15 = level 615 (about 150 nits) is the
     HyperOS default.

     Until 2.22 the map stopped at 500 nits and there was no <highBrightnessMode>, so the framework
     capped brightness at 500 nits and the HBM half of the range was unreachable (hbmMode=off in
     every log; flashlight test 18.11: 43 420 lux, brt=1.0, nits=500). The lights patch also sent
     1..2047, so the middle of the slider was twice darker than stock. With the block below the cap
     is transitionPoint while the ambient light is dim and 1.0 (1000 nits) from 6001 lux up, which is
     how the stock ROM reaches 1000 nits. The auto-brightness curve in FrameworksResOverlayEmerald is
     in nits and was resampled from the stock one, so it keeps giving the same brightness below
     500 nits and climbs to ~826 nits at 45 000 lux - no step at the HBM threshold.

     Differences from the stock file: thermalStatusLimit is dropped, this framework version has no
     such field (unknown elements are skipped; HBM is bounded by the regular brightness throttling
     instead). The timing limits are not the stock zeros: the stock ROM leaves HBM timing to the
     vendor service (hbmKeepOnMaxTime 1800 s, hbmRestTime 600 s), and that path is dead here (it
     writes /sys/class/mi_display/disp-DSI-0/backlight, an attribute this kernel does not have), so
     the framework enforces its own budget: at most 1800 s of HBM per hour, half the vendor duty
     cycle. The thermalThrottling block caps brightness by thermal status, which also drops HBM: a
     cap at the transition point means "no HBM", since the controller only keeps HBM while brightness
     is above it. Horizon values as stock. -->
<displayConfiguration>
    <screenBrightnessMap>
        <point>
            <value>0.001709819</value>
            <nits>2.0</nits>
        </point>
        <point>
            <value>0.49975574</value>
            <nits>500.0</nits>
        </point>
        <point>
            <value>1.0</value>
            <nits>1000.0</nits>
        </point>
    </screenBrightnessMap>
    <thermalThrottling>
        <brightnessThrottlingMap>
            <brightnessThrottlingPoint>
                <thermalStatus>severe</thermalStatus>
                <brightness>0.49975574</brightness>
            </brightnessThrottlingPoint>
            <brightnessThrottlingPoint>
                <thermalStatus>critical</thermalStatus>
                <brightness>0.3</brightness>
            </brightnessThrottlingPoint>
        </brightnessThrottlingMap>
    </thermalThrottling>
    <highBrightnessMode enabled="true">
        <transitionPoint>0.49975574</transitionPoint>
        <minimumLux>6001</minimumLux>
        <timing>
            <timeWindowSecs>3600</timeWindowSecs>
            <timeMaxSecs>1800</timeMaxSecs>
            <timeMinSecs>60</timeMinSecs>
        </timing>
        <allowInLowPowerMode>true</allowInLowPowerMode>
        <minimumHdrPercentOfScreen>0</minimumHdrPercentOfScreen>
        <sdrHdrRatioMap>
            <point>
                <sdrNits>2.0</sdrNits>
                <hdrRatio>1</hdrRatio>
            </point>
            <point>
                <sdrNits>1000.0</sdrNits>
                <hdrRatio>1</hdrRatio>
            </point>
        </sdrHdrRatioMap>
    </highBrightnessMode>
    <ambientLightHorizonLong>3000</ambientLightHorizonLong>
    <ambientLightHorizonShort>1000</ambientLightHorizonShort>
</displayConfiguration>
